input.content:
Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an polymorphism task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: Your guild needs a flexible spell-casting system. Implement polymorphism by overriding the `cast` method in specific spell classes. Each spell should describe its unique effect while also using its inherited mana cost.

Current code in the editor:
```
class Spell {
  constructor(name, manaCost) {
    this.name = name;
    this.manaCost = manaCost;
  }

  // TODO: Implement a generic cast method using the spell's name and mana cost.
  cast() {
    return "A generic spell is cast.";
  }
}

class FireballSpell extends Spell {
  constructor(manaCost, damage) {
    // TODO: Call the parent constructor correctly with the name "Fireball".
    super();
    this.damage = damage;
  }

  // TODO: Override the cast method to describe a Fireball's effect, including its damage and mana cost.
  cast() {
    return "This spell launches a fiery projectile!";
  }
}

class HealSpell extends Spell {
  constructor(manaCost, healAmount) {
    // TODO: Call the parent constructor correctly with the name "Heal".
    super();
    this.healAmount = healAmount;
  }

  // TODO: Override the cast method to describe a Heal spell's effect, including its heal amount and mana cost.
  cast() {
    return "This spell mends wounds!";
  }
}

```

